id: migrations/2026-09-12-cohere-vocabulary-and-attribution
title: "Cohere the vocabulary, attribute the records, surface the decisions"
kind: migration-receipt
record_shape: header
status: active
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; changes proposed from JUDGMENTS.md and accepted by Dave in conversation; not a mass rewrite"
updated: 2026-09-13
supersedes: none
inventory_ref: JUDGMENTS.md

purpose: >
  Record what changed, what was deliberately left alone, and how to undo it.
  The judgment inventory of 2026-09-12 found the repository stating rules it
  did not enforce and enforcing rules it did not state. This receipt closes the
  gap by adding checks, not by rewriting history: every existing divergent value
  is grandfathered by file, every ledger may only shrink, and no record's
  meaning was changed.

what_changed:
  vocabulary:
    - change: "top-level status: closed to the lifecycle enum draft|active|superseded|archived|deleted"
      enforced_by: tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs
      grandfathered: "145 files, by name, frozen; ceiling 145; the ledger may only shrink"
      why: >
        38 distinct values were in use across 176 files, mixing lifecycle,
        version, authority, and loop position in one field the schema keeps as
        eight. templates/basic.yawn now teaches the enum on its status: line.
    - change: "authored_by: field with enum dave-human|agent-on-behalf|yawn.bot|unattributed and authored_via:"
      enforced_by: tests/authored-by.test.mjs
      required_on: [decisions/, dave/, records/yawn.bot-state.yawn]
      why: >
        100 of 194 .yawn files were last written by the yawn.ai git identity,
        which shares the maintainer's email; the tree could not say whether a
        stated preference was Dave's. The field says who is answerable.
    - change: "record_shape: declared in every template; templates/node.yawn ranks five shapes and names header canonical"
      enforced_by: tests/record-shape.test.mjs
      why: "four incompatible shapes with no statement of which was canonical"
  proof:
    - change: "proof: blocks must resolve every path they cite; covers: and not_covered: convention"
      enforced_by: scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs
      first_applied: core/canonical-extension.yawn
      why: >
        The canonical-extension proof named a validator that checks the alias
        list and nothing else, while the record also claims media_role and case.
        Its proof now says what it covers and lists the two claims it does not.
      grandfathered: "2 files citing a private Windows filesystem, by name, frozen; ceiling 2"
  manifest:
    - change: "yawn.yawn link tables kept complete against the filesystem"
      enforced_by: scripts/generate-manifest.mjs (check mode in npm run validate)
      applied: "54 missing links appended; no existing entry rewritten or removed"
  entities:
    - added: core/entity-and-coupling.yawn
      why: >
        Names the principal, the runtime, and a third entity whose name is held;
        defines the slash as a relationship record; carries the settled answer
        to the role question with its why and a recall rule.
  decisions:
    - added: decisions/
      count: "52 records from the reversal axes, numbered by leverage, plus 053 held"
      rule: "every record is proposed with an empty choice:; a recommendation carries authority: none"
    - added: records/yawn.bot-state.yawn
      generated_by: scripts/render-bot-state.mjs
      why: "a surface needs one record to read; the contracts said daily while the newest ledger entry was 2026-07-04"
    - added: dave/orientation/
      why: "the settled role drops from the top slot; the next highest-leverage question takes it"
  runtime_pointer:
    - change: "official_runtime.repository and agents/yawn.bot.yawn identity.repository corrected from yawn-ai/web-game to yawn-ai/yawn.bot"
      why: >
        Dave stated on 2026-09-12 that web-game is the older repository and is to
        be archived, and that yawn.bot with its Supabase database is the runtime.
        At the time of the change both repositories were at the same commit
        (a0ff2f4), so the correction is one of address, not content.
      epistemic_status: reported
      old_address_kept_as: superseded_repository
    - change: "the remaining active records that named web-game as the runtime now name yawn.bot: examples/cold-start-agent.yawn, scripts/verify-cold-start.ps1, q-space/node.yawn, questions/open-questions.yawn"
      applied: 2026-09-13
      why: >
        The 2026-07-11 repository-slug question in questions/open-questions.yawn
        is answered by the same statement and moved to recently_resolved as
        answered-provisionally (reported, recorded on Dave's behalf); the
        2026-07-11 answer naming web-game is marked superseded, not deleted.
        One open question replaces it: when web-game is archived and which
        links must move first. Historical records (the 2026-07-11 promotion
        receipt, the cold-start proof, the drift ledger, the MVB-1 deliverable)
        keep the old address as history.
  runtime_surface:
    - change: "yawn.bot/dave and its chat view read a vendored, pinned copy of records/yawn.bot-state.yawn"
      where: "yawn-ai/yawn.bot pull request 157, branch claude/dave-next-question-r0ysdf; this repository's pull request 33 carries the record"
      what_the_surface_shows: >
        The next highest-leverage open decision first, then the ranked queue,
        then Dave's own inquiries, then the judgments he has made; the settled
        role is recalled from principal_role_settled with its why and is the
        purpose vector of the page; the two support expanders appear only under
        judgments. The header status there still comes from Supabase
        connectivity, not from observed_activity.
      pin_rule: "the runtime pins the record's git blob in protocol/dot-yawn.lock.json; a stale pin is bumped there by a reviewed change"
      epistemic_status: observed
      proof: "yawn.bot tests/unit/dave-public-mission.test.tsx, tests/unit/yawn-bot-state-record.test.ts, tests/e2e/dave-public-model.spec.ts"
      merged:
        this_repository: "pull request 33 merged 2026-09-13 as c3de16b5f345209ed7ad04a11ee6f6652ee6c349 on main (merge commit; hosted CI passed on the merged head)"
        runtime: "yawn-ai/yawn.bot pull request 157 merged 2026-09-13 as 21f086a5598e58356630ffbb0de2fe8f6a0e883b on main; its lock pins this record at blob 59198132b895d506d67c41ddc4da25b89d6cf7f1, upstreamCommit c3de16b5, upstreamStatus merged"
        authorized_by: "Dave, in conversation on 2026-09-13; recorded on his behalf"
        runtime_receipt: "yawn.bot YAWNS/Observations/YAWN_DAVE_NEXT_QUESTION_MERGE_2026_09_13.yawn"
        not_observed: "the production page after the merge; the session's network egress refuses yawn.bot and the GitHub integration cannot read deployment statuses, so the live result is Dave's to look at"
  entry:
    - added: CLAUDE.md
      why: "one file that is true on landing, for agents"
    - added: "CONTRIBUTING.md Attribution section and Authored-By commit trailer"
  validate_script: >
    npm run validate now also runs generate-manifest (check),
    validate-proof-refs, and render-bot-state --check. CI runs npm test,
    which runs validate first.

review_followup:
  date: 2026-09-13
  source: "adversarial review workflow run over the merged change set; findings verified by reproduction before being applied"
  applied:
    - "scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs inspects every column-0 proof: block, not only the first; detects a drive-letter or file: path anywhere on a line, not only at its start; resolves cited paths of any extension, directories, and paths with a #fragment; the external-source ledger is a frozen snapshot that may only shrink"
    - "tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs checks every column-0 status: line and the grandfather ledger is a frozen snapshot (tests/fixtures/status-grandfather-2026-09-12.txt, sha256 pinned) so a freed slot cannot be reused"
    - "templates/open-question.yawn: the question's own state is question_status:, so a template no longer teaches a second top-level status:"
    - "tests/record-shape.test.mjs: end-of-input anchor instead of a literal Z"
    - "scripts/render-bot-state.mjs: a decision with a filled choice.selected_by or a superseded, archived, or deleted status is not open and leaves the queue; the default date is today's, not a literal"
    - "records/cold-start-proof-2026-07-11.yawn marked superseded by this receipt; the corrected fixture is not re-run (no Windows host), so a fresh receipt is owed"
    - "dave/node.yawn and the two mental-model records: authored_via now states the original provenance instead of naming a git author the same commit replaced; updated: bumped"
    - "yawn.yawn and agents/yawn.bot.yawn updated: bumped to the day they were edited"
    - "JUDGMENTS.md dates its coverage claim to main 09933cb; the records this change set added are not inventoried"
    - "two decision falsifiers no longer quote a literal drive path inside proof:"
    - "CONTRIBUTING.md: the Authored-By trailer applies from 2026-09-13 forward and trailers must be one contiguous block"
    - "this receipt: three tests, three scripts, three validate steps; render-bot-state --check named"
    - "tests/decisions.test.mjs: leverage equals the printed formula inputs, numbering follows leverage, no choice is filled unless the record is superseded, every recommendation carries authority none, every judgment id cited under decisions/ resolves in TAXONOMY.md; decisions/node.yawn names it"
    - "tests/render-bot-state.test.mjs: the renderer reads a fixture root (YAWN_ROOT) and a chosen or superseded decision leaves the queue; a non-numeric leverage stops the render"
    - "decisions/*: state_snapshot.attributed_to and source.id_index name TAXONOMY.md, where the judgment ids resolve; resolves: renamed evidence_sample: because it is a sample, not the axis count the formula uses; no record quotes a literal drive path"
    - "templates/decision.yawn regenerated from the shape the records carry (header keys, axis, poles, split, leverage and its formula, options with evidence_for, recommendation with authority none, evidence_sample)"
    - "JUDGMENTS.md: #3 and #385 retagged REVEALED · BP as its own §4 had found (TAXONOMY.md rows J1177 and J1216 retagged with them; neither axis feeds a decision record's leverage: ontology-ambition is not a reversal axis and vocabulary-closure keeps two other authored rows on the same pole); the verification and coverage claims are pinned to main 09933cb; §2 no longer calls the stated side the author's; §6 says its columns sum to 2316 because a judgment anchored to n files appears in n rows"
    - "HOLDOUT.md and HOLDOUT_METHOD.md: the pre-registration ordering is stated as the author's report (method and result landed in one commit, 4262644); the selection draw is in tests/fixtures/holdout-files.txt and holdout-selection.json; the committed leak remedy is applied in a disclosed line (precision 0.325, recall 0.231 after dropping the three files read across groups) while the headline keeps all 20"
    - "dave/orientation: the inventory claim carries the commit and date on both the record and its page"
  not_applied:
    - "recomputing the header counts of JUDGMENTS.md for the two retagged records; the header says so"

not_migrated:
  - what: "the 145 grandfathered status: values"
    why: "rewriting them is a per-record judgment (is v0-seed draft or active?), not a mechanical one; each migrates when its record is next touched, and the ledger shrinks"
  - what: "the 15 references to C:/Users/dave/... in active records"
    why: "external workspace paths; renaming Dave's folder is not this receipt's to decide; the case and reachability questions are decisions/ records"
  - what: "record shapes of existing instances"
    why: "declared and ranked, not converted; a shape migration needs its own receipt with fixtures"
  - what: "the container entity's name"
    why: "held under core/canonical-extension.yawn creation_gate.on_ambiguity; decisions/053"
  - what: "the yawn.bot/dave header status dropdown"
    why: "it lives in the runtime repository and still reads Supabase connectivity; the page body and the chat view read this repository's bot-state record as of yawn-ai/yawn.bot pull request 157 (see runtime_surface)"
  - what: "archiving yawn-ai/web-game"
    why: "an outward-facing GitHub action for Dave to take; the intent is recorded in questions/open-questions.yawn"

rollback: >
  Every change is additive and lives in named files. Remove the three tests
  (status-vocabulary, authored-by, record-shape), the three scripts
  (validate-proof-refs, generate-manifest, render-bot-state), and the three
  package.json validate steps and the previous suite passes unchanged. The 54 manifest links are appended at block ends and can be
  deleted as a range. record_shape:, authored_by:, and authored_via: lines can
  be stripped by a one-line filter. decisions/, dave/orientation/, CLAUDE.md,
  and core/entity-and-coupling.yawn are new paths. No record's prior content
  was rewritten except templates/basic.yawn (three header lines added) and
  core/canonical-extension.yawn (covers/not_covered added under proof:).

provenance:
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  merge_record: TAXONOMY.md
  holdout: HOLDOUT.md
  method: HOLDOUT_METHOD.md

proof:
  covers:
    - what_changed
    - not_migrated
    - rollback
  condition: "npm test passes on the tree this receipt describes, including the three new test files and the check-mode validators"
  tests:
    - tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs
    - tests/authored-by.test.mjs
    - tests/record-shape.test.mjs
  validators:
    - scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs
    - scripts/generate-manifest.mjs
    - scripts/render-bot-state.mjs
  status: contract-defined
